king modifications or cancellations as per user's instruction.\n\nNow, considering the tools available, the first step is to get the user's details to find their recent reservation. So the first tool call should be get_user_details with the provided user ID. Then, based on the response, retrieve the reservation details to check the passenger count and flight status. If the flight was delayed, check if compensation criteria are met (e.g., membership level, insurance, cabin class). If so, offer the certificate. If not, explain why. Then, when the user says they'll call back, end the interaction without proceeding with the booking.\n</think>\n\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"get_user_details\", \"arguments\": {\"user_id\": \"noah_muller_9847\"}}\n",
